  "summary": "Skye Kakoschke-Moore, a senator for the Nick Xenophon Team (NXT), is resigning from the Australian Senate due to holding dual British citizenship by descent. She discovered she possessed this citizenship through her mother, who was born in Singapore, a former British colony.  Kakoschke-Moore had previously believed she was not British after receiving advice at age 12 from the British embassy.  Her mother, born in 1957, acquired \"citizenship of the United Kingdom and colonies\" and later became a British citizen in 1983 under the British Nationality Act, which Kakoschke-Moore then inherited by descent.  She expressed significant surprise and heartbreak at this revelation. Kakoschke-Moore intends to request the high court determine how her Senate vacancy will be filled and plans to continue her political career with the NXT, aiming to return to the Senate.  A recount of the 2016 election is anticipated to result in Tim Storrer filling the vacancy, although the NXT's leader, Nick Xenophon, has indicated preliminary legal advice suggests the process might be more complex and \"uncharted legal territory,\" referencing a recent high court decision. Xenophon stated he and his colleagues are \"devastated\" by her departure but believe this is not the conclusion of her political journey."
}
